      "statement": "A Generation is everything a node derives from a deployment — compiled Worker configurations, isolate pools, the Durable Object class registry, the service-binding graph, asset resolvers, and the cron schedule. A node serves exactly one current generation and reaches it through a snapshot, so a request started on one generation finishes on it even after the node adopts another.",
